# Axum proxy

- Stream upstream NDJSON or SSE. Do not buffer the full response.
- Cap request bodies **before** buffering.
- Retry another node **only pre-first-byte** (connect/timeout/overload statuses).
  Once a stream has begun, never retry.
- Rewrite `/api/embeddings` → `/api/embed` (Ollama ≤0.32 compat, not debt).
  Do **not** rewrite `/v1/embeddings`.
- `GET /api/tags` is a **CLI-compatible union** across healthy nodes (digest
  ≥12 chars; placeholder SHA-256 of the name when the probe omitted digest).
  `GET /v1/models` and `GET /v1/models/{id}` use the same union.
- Capacity / saturation / no-healthy → **503** + `Retry-After`. Body shape
  follows the request path (Ollama string on `/api/*`, OpenAI envelope on `/v1/*`).
- Nonretryable pre-response upstream failures → **502**, not raw framework errors.
- `IncrementalCollector`: cap an unterminated frame at **1 MiB**; never alter forwarded chunks.
- Never log bodies. `inflight_inc` only on POST inference (native generate/chat/embed
  and OpenAI chat/completions/embeddings).

```rust
// BAD — retry after streaming started
while let Some(chunk) = stream.next().await {
    if chunk.is_err() { return retry_other_node().await; }
}

// GOOD — retry only before first byte; then pipe
let resp = client.send().await?; // retryable here
let mut stream = resp.bytes_stream(); // not retryable after this
```

See `.opencode/wiki/concepts/ollama-router-phase-3-retry-and-memory-safety.md`.
Skill: `ollama-compat-proxy`.
